{"title":"2025 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Simple_Vectors)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Simple Vectors)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Helpful_Diagram\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Helpful Diagram</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~0:50)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:50)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Quick_and_Simple)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Quick and Simple)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_(Fast_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2  (Fast and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Frances stands <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> meters directly south of a locked gate in a fence that runs east-west. Immediately behind the fence is a box of chocolates, located <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> meters east of the locked gate. An unlocked gate lies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> meters east of the box, and another unlocked gate lies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> meters west of the locked gate. Frances can reach the box by walking toward an unlocked gate, passing through it, and walking toward the box. It happens that the total distance Frances would travel is the same via either unlocked gate. What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/2/1123efff170b8350004c9b2855ee21c8209171ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 3 \\frac{2}{7} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 3 \\frac{3}{7} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 3 \\frac{4}{7} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 3 \\frac{5}{7} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 3 \\frac{6}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"416\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let Frances's location be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, the locked gate be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, the box be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, the unlocked gate on the west be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />, and the unlocked gate on the east be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\nWe are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/5/b1514755b36a5ddefab9527163b40e1e903907b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FL = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/f/99f710bb9558eb265f39cc95cb248e6235a1c6a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LB = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc9b04270bc2252040311c5d93719a5098da0518.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BV$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> = 9, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/2/bc20d34584018148e8f79b3412ea90e90dca3100.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LU = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/c/8ccd6bdfd1c8b22e53cab5a58b25f0680f2fc62f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FL$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is vertical and the fence is horizontal, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7b3a5dbc2ba07bb14715deaf94bc94ac4f7a6c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle FLU = m \\angle FLV = 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"216\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>If Frances takes the western path, she must first travel the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/e/8ee093245073684099c51099e3e11d86379f73aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FV$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/d/33df0f509a29f8fdc933c9e46da57a0d1f00f69f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> meters. By the Pythagorean theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/d/fad65c5e311bca7479161d1368c80cc5667b7eb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FV = \\sqrt{8^2 + 15^2} = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"177\" height=\"21\" />. The remaining distance from Francis and the box of chocolates after she walks that distance is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/3/f333028a7c846fb4c28628a04e115f3c6da81c19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 + x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> meters. Thus, the distance Francis travels if she takes the western path is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/2/ea2b644cb911b7e4a1e9adbdca9ef1d2c6a8844f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 + x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>If Frances takes the eastern path, she first travels <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/0/fb0396841df3b70ff38a77853b139b691840d039.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(x + 9)^2 + 15^2} = \\sqrt{(x + 9)^2 + 225}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"286\" height=\"35\" /> meters, and then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more meters. Her total distance on the eastern path is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/4/a44812aebdd202bdf2f1bf9849e6c2ffd4c7ba3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(x + 9)^2 + 225} + 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"164\" height=\"35\" /> meters.\n</p><p>Now, setting the two distances equal to each other yields:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/3/573a53c698d98af6b07abbae86fad9f3b825efa8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}&amp;\\qquad\\;\\;\\;\\; x + 25 = \\sqrt{(x + 9)^2 + 225} + 9 \\\\ &amp;\\iff x + 16 = \\sqrt{(x + 9)^2 + 225} \\\\ &amp;\\iff x^2 + 32x + 256 = (x + 9)^2 + 225 \\\\ &amp;\\iff x^2 + 32x + 256 = x^2 + 18x + 81 + 225 \\\\ &amp;\\iff 14x = 50 \\\\ &amp;\\iff x = \\frac{50}{14} = \\frac{25}{7}.\\end{align*}\" width=\"342\" height=\"195\" />\nThis means the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/4/0548018fd86c78ffbb77c2248065264dc5de5a23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{25}{7} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\hspace{3pt}3\\frac{4}{7}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"150\" height=\"49\" />. \n</p><p>~Milkdrinker\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Simple_Vectors.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Simple_Vectors)\">Solution 2 (Simple Vectors)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Simple Vectors)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/c/eac6afc3c30d7bee3ef0911ed62b8b8508e322e4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[F = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ -15 \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad B = \\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad E = \\begin{pmatrix} x+9 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad W = \\begin{pmatrix} -8 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix},\\]\" width=\"462\" height=\"43\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/e/cae4fd68f44ac9b909f8d91f9d498de5759bb45b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> since the box (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />) lies to the east (i.e. in the positive horizontal direction) of the locked gate.\nThe paths’ lengths are then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69204e4a965167a8c23de0351801c8ffa475ed6e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[D_E = \\|E - F\\|_2 + \\|B - E\\|_2, \\quad D_W = \\|W - F\\|_2 + \\|B - W\\|_2.\\]\" width=\"494\" height=\"18\" />\nCompute:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/b/b0b0b2a1b0903f5ad0b9e96f31c26e034d9bed5b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\|E - F\\|_2 = \\sqrt{(x+9)^2 + 15^2}, \\quad \\|B - E\\|_2 = \\sqrt{9^2} = 9, \\quad \\|W - F\\|_2 = \\sqrt{(-8)^2 + 15^2} = 17, \\quad \\|B - W\\|_2 = |x+8| = x+8 \\quad\\text{(as } x &gt; 0 \\text{)}.\\]\" width=\"999\" height=\"32\" />\nSet \\( D_E = D_W \\):\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dc3b1eed83c2da2284e288fd13b3696906e1ae6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{(x+9)^2 + 225} + 9 = 17 + (x+8) \\iff \\sqrt{(x+9)^2 + 225} = x+16.\\]\" width=\"536\" height=\"32\" />\nSquare both sides (noting that both sides are indeed non-negative, again as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/e/cae4fd68f44ac9b909f8d91f9d498de5759bb45b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />):\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/0/8a0380df843cd29d8498bd43ad72995585553036.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}&amp;~~(x+9)^2 + 225 = (x+16)^2 \\iff x^2 + 18x + 306 = x^2 + 32x + 256 \\\\ &amp;\\iff 14x = 50 \\iff x = \\frac{25}{7}.\\end{align*}\" width=\"522\" height=\"64\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, our answer is \\( \\frac{25}{7} \\) or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/0/b0091aba75f22b8abddb05b75e192040b718e16e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\hspace{3pt}3\\frac{4}{7}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"69\" height=\"49\" />. \n</p><p>~notvalid\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Helpful_Diagram\">Helpful Diagram</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Helpful Diagram\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a0530f97e46bef12c8459a2e4fb98a98478f9765.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(10cm);  // Points pair F = (0,-15); pair L = (0,0); pair W = (-8,0); pair B = (25/7,0); pair E = (25/7+9,0);  // Fence draw((-20,0)--(20,0), linewidth(1));  // Paths draw(F--W--B, linewidth(1)); draw(F--E--B, linewidth(1));  // Points dot(F); dot(L); dot(W); dot(B); dot(E);  // Labels for points label(&quot;F&quot;, F, S); label(&quot;L&quot;, L, N); label(&quot;W&quot;, W, N); label(&quot;B&quot;, B, N); label(&quot;E&quot;, E, N);  // Distances and Labels for Distances draw((0,0)--(0,-15), dashed); label(&quot;15&quot;, (-5.5,-5.5), E);  draw(W--L, dashed); label(&quot;8&quot;, (-4,0.5), N);  draw(L--B, dashed); label(&quot;$x$&quot;, ((L.x+B.x)/2,0.5), N);  draw(B--E, dashed); label(&quot;9&quot;, ((B.x+E.x)/2,0.5), N); [/asy]\" width=\"475\" height=\"228\" />\n</p><p>~JerryZYang\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_.28Logical.2C_Good_Editing.2C_.7E0:50.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~0:50)\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:50)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:50)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/kuCphxoN2do\">https://www.youtube.com/shorts/kuCphxoN2do</a>\n</p><p>~Ebai\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/vayQuXXbr28\">https://youtu.be/vayQuXXbr28</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.28Quick_and_Simple.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(Quick_and_Simple)\">Video Solution(Quick and Simple)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(Quick and Simple)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3JMxreduYM4\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3JMxreduYM4</a>\n~Sigma_Bob\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dLSWVrrKsgs\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dLSWVrrKsgs</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_2_.28Fast_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_(Fast_and_Easy)\">Video Solution 2  (Fast and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2  (Fast and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qsO702m4r64\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qsO702m4r64</a>\n~ Pi Academy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable